## The Week at a Glance

- 🔴 **Teams and email attacks are evolving faster than traditional defenses:** Threat actors are abandoning disrupted phishing platforms and pivoting to Teams-based social engineering and automated, multi-stage attack chains, meaning your employees are now a target in chat, not just in their inbox.
- 🟡 **AI agents now need their own security layer:** Microsoft is previewing runtime threat detection for AI agents that can access enterprise data and take actions autonomously; organizations deploying Copilot or custom agents should plan to evaluate these new controls before broader agent adoption accelerates.
- 🟡 **Purview data retention billing is changing:** How Microsoft charges for Data Lifecycle Management is shifting to a volume-based model, which could meaningfully affect your compliance budget if you retain large volumes of AI-generated content.
- 🟢 **Microsoft Entra now backs up your identity directory automatically:** Tenant backup and recovery for Entra ID is now on by default, closing a significant gap in identity resilience with no immediate action required.

*Sources: [Microsoft Security Blog - Q2 2026 Email Threat Landscape](https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/07/23/email-threat-landscape-q2-2026-trends-and-insights/) · [Microsoft Defender for Endpoint Blog - Securing AI Agents at Runtime](https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/microsoft-security-community/securing-ai-agents-at-runtime-real-time-protection-and-threat/ba-p/4541255) · [Entra What's New - July 2026](https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/microsoft-entra-blog/what-s-new-in-microsoft-entra-july-2026/ba-p/4534631)*

---

## Why This Week Matters

The convergence of two trends this week demands leadership attention: attackers are deliberately moving onto collaboration platforms where defenses are weaker, and AI agents are expanding the attack surface inside your own environment at the same time. Organizations that have invested in email security but not yet extended that scrutiny to Teams communications and AI agent behavior face a widening blind spot. The decisions made in the next 30 to 60 days about AI agent governance and collaboration platform security controls will define your exposure for the rest of this year.

*Sources: [Microsoft Security Blog - Rethinking Security for the Age of AI](https://blogs.microsoft.com/blog/2026/07/27/rethinking-security-for-the-age-of-ai/) · [Microsoft Security Blog - Q2 2026 Email Threat Landscape](https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/07/23/email-threat-landscape-q2-2026-trends-and-insights/)*

---

## Risk & Compliance

- 🔴 **[Teams-based social engineering on the rise - Q2 2026 threat report](https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/07/23/email-threat-landscape-q2-2026-trends-and-insights/):** Following Microsoft's disruption of the Tycoon2FA phishing platform, threat actors have pivoted to Teams-based social engineering and multi-stage automated attacks, meaning your existing email security investment no longer covers the full attack surface; review Teams external access policies and user awareness training now. Relevant to HIPAA, SOC 2, and CMMC; act within 30 days.

- 🔴 **[July 2026 Exchange Server security updates released](https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/exchange-team-blog/released-july-2026-exchange-server-security-updates/ba-p/4534146):** Microsoft has released security updates for Exchange Server SE, 2019, and 2016 addressing vulnerabilities reported by external security partners; organizations running on-premises Exchange must apply these patches immediately to close known exploitable gaps. Note that Exchange 2019 and 2016 require enrollment in the Period 2 Extended Security Update program to access these fixes.

- 🟡 **[AI agent runtime security now available in preview](https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/microsoft-security-community/securing-ai-agents-at-runtime-real-time-protection-and-threat/ba-p/4541255):** AI agents operating in Microsoft 365 can now access data, call tools, and take actions autonomously, creating attack paths that traditional controls were not designed to address; Microsoft Defender for Microsoft Agent 365 now offers preview-stage runtime threat detection and protection for these workflows. Organizations with active Copilot or Copilot Studio deployments should evaluate enrollment before agent use expands further.

- 🟡 **[Purview Data Lifecycle Management billing model changing](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=560324):** DLM billing is shifting from a per-message to a volume-based model charged at $0.25 per GB per month, which will directly affect compliance budgets for any organization retaining AI-generated prompts and responses at scale; finance and compliance teams should model expected data volumes against the new pricing before the change takes effect.

- 🟡 **[Entra custom sign-in branding will begin retiring CSS positioning in October 2026](https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/microsoft-entra-blog/microsoft-entra-id-enhances-security-of-branded-sign-ins/ba-p/4537471):** Microsoft is retiring custom CSS positioning properties from Entra sign-in pages on October 26, 2026 as part of its Secure Future Initiative, with full CSS retirement planned for 2027; organizations with customized sign-in pages should audit their branding configurations and plan updates before the October deadline to avoid visible disruption to users. This change strengthens phishing resistance by reducing attacker ability to manipulate the sign-in UI surface.

- 🟡 **[Microsoft Entra Backup and Recovery now on by default](https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/microsoft-entra-blog/what-s-new-in-microsoft-entra-july-2026/ba-p/4534631):** Entra ID now automatically backs up critical directory objects including users, groups, Conditional Access policies, and managed identities, enabling tenant restoration after accidental or malicious changes; this closes a meaningful identity resilience gap relevant to SOC 2 and NIST CSF with no configuration required, but organizations should confirm their recovery procedures reference this new capability. This closes an implicit-trust gap by ensuring that even compromised or maliciously altered identity configurations can be reliably restored.

- 🟢 **[People Skills admin deletion control now available](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=565905):** Administrators can now permanently delete all People Skills data from the tenant, supporting GDPR and internal data governance requirements for organizations that need to offboard from the feature or respond to data subject requests.

- 🟢 **[SharePoint auto-labeling for data at rest coming in preview September 2026](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=559105):** A new capability will automatically apply default sensitivity labels to existing unlabeled SharePoint files, closing labeling gaps for data at rest without requiring user action; preview in September, generally available in October 2026. Relevant to organizations with HIPAA, GDPR, or information protection requirements who have struggled with manual labeling compliance.

*Sources: [Microsoft Security Blog - Q2 2026 Email Threat Landscape](https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/07/23/email-threat-landscape-q2-2026-trends-and-insights/) · [Entra What's New - July 2026](https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/microsoft-entra-blog/what-s-new-in-microsoft-entra-july-2026/ba-p/4534631) · [M365 Roadmap - Purview DLM Meter Change](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=560324)*

