## What Your Employees Will Notice

- **New Copilot voice notes on mobile (August 2026):** Employees with Microsoft 365 Copilot licenses will be able to record voice notes in the Copilot mobile app and have them converted into structured, searchable content, which is useful for capturing meeting follow-ups or ideas while away from a desk.
- **Copilot search suggestions in Outlook have been cancelled:** Microsoft has decided not to proceed with Copilot search suggestions in the Outlook search menu; no user-facing change will occur, but employees who read about this feature should know it is no longer coming.
- **Teams inline search via @mention has been deferred:** The feature enabling @mention-based file and channel search inside the compose box has been cancelled for now; employees who saw roadmap previews should be informed it will not arrive.
- **Anthropic Claude Opus 5 now available in Copilot:** Employees using Microsoft 365 Copilot can now select Claude Opus 5 as their model for complex, multi-step tasks across Word, Excel, and other apps, expanding the choice of AI reasoning engines available in daily work.
- **Viva Engage community feeds are being improved (September 2026):** Feed sorting and content review behavior in Viva Engage communities will update to better match how employees naturally read and triage messages.
- **New profile cards for buildings, rooms, and desks in Copilot Chat:** Employees will see richer directory cards for workplace locations when searching through Copilot Chat or other Microsoft 365 entry points, making room and desk discovery easier.

*Sources: [M365 Roadmap - Copilot Voice Notes](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=498640) · [M365 Copilot Blog - Claude Opus 5](https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/microsoft-365-copilot-blog/available-today-anthropic-claude-opus-5-in-microsoft-365-copilot/ba-p/4540524) · [M365 Roadmap - Viva Engage Feed Improvements](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=513275)*

---

## What Your Help Desk Should Expect

- **Teams external access questions:** As awareness of Teams-based social engineering grows, expect employees to ask how to identify and report suspicious Teams messages from external senders, particularly if you communicate this threat to staff.
- **Exchange patch tickets:** IT staff applying the July 2026 Exchange Server security updates should anticipate potential restart windows and temporary service interruptions; communicate scheduled maintenance in advance to reduce inbound tickets.
- **Copilot mobile voice notes support requests (August):** When voice notes arrive in the Copilot mobile app, help desk should prepare for questions about supported operating systems, language availability, and where to find recorded notes.
- **Claude Opus 5 model selection questions:** Some employees may not know how to switch AI models inside Copilot; a brief how-to communication can reduce inbound requests.
- **People Skills deletion inquiries:** If your organization chooses to exercise the new admin deletion control for People Skills data, users will notice skills disappearing from their profile cards; proactive communication before deletion is initiated will reduce confusion.
- **Entra sign-in branding changes (October deadline):** If your IT team has customized the Entra sign-in page using CSS, they should begin testing now; end users may notice visual changes if branding is not updated before the October 26 deadline.

*Sources: [Exchange Team Blog - July 2026 Security Updates](https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/exchange-team-blog/released-july-2026-exchange-server-security-updates/ba-p/4534146) · [Entra Blog - Enhanced Branded Sign-Ins](https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/microsoft-entra-blog/microsoft-entra-id-enhances-security-of-branded-sign-ins/ba-p/4537471) · [M365 Roadmap - People Skills Deletion Control](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=565905)*

