## Cost & Licensing

- **Purview Data Lifecycle Management pricing shift:** The move to volume-based billing at $0.25 per GB per month will affect any organization using DLM policies to retain AI-generated content, including Copilot prompts and responses. Organizations retaining high volumes of AI interactions should model their expected GB per month against current per-message costs to identify whether this represents a budget increase before the change takes effect.
- **GitHub Copilot spend visibility via Viva Insights (Preview):** Managers with five or more direct reports can now view GitHub Copilot usage and spend data in Viva Insights dashboards, giving leadership a practical tool to assess return on AI licensing investment before making renewal or expansion decisions.
- **Claude Opus 5 included in existing Copilot license:** Access to Anthropic Claude Opus 5 inside Microsoft 365 Copilot requires no additional licensing purchase; it is available to existing Copilot license holders as an additional model choice.

*Sources: [M365 Roadmap - DLM Meter Change](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=560324) · [M365 Roadmap - Viva Insights for GitHub Copilot](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=566470) · [M365 Copilot Blog - Claude Opus 5](https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/microsoft-365-copilot-blog/available-today-anthropic-claude-opus-5-in-microsoft-365-copilot/ba-p/4540524)*

---

## Planning Horizon

- **Immediately - [July 2026 Exchange Server security updates](https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/exchange-team-blog/released-july-2026-exchange-server-security-updates/ba-p/4534146):** Confirm your IT team has applied or scheduled the July 2026 security updates for all on-premises Exchange servers, and verify Exchange 2019 or 2016 environments are enrolled in the Period 2 ESU program or begin migration planning now.

- **Within 14 days - [Teams-based social engineering threat response](https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/07/23/email-threat-landscape-q2-2026-trends-and-insights/):** Review your organization's Teams external access policies and schedule a user awareness communication so employees know how to recognize and report suspicious messages arriving via Teams chat, not just email.

- **Within 30 days - [AI agent runtime security evaluation](https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/microsoft-security-community/securing-ai-agents-at-runtime-real-time-protection-and-threat/ba-p/4541255):** Task your security team with evaluating Microsoft Defender for Microsoft Agent 365 preview controls before autonomous agent use expands across the business; establish a governance policy for what agents are permitted to access and act upon.

- **Within 30 days - [Purview DLM billing model impact assessment](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=560324):** Have your compliance and finance teams estimate retained AI-generated content volumes in GB to model the cost impact of the new volume-based billing and identify any budget adjustment needed.

- **Before October 26, 2026 - [Entra custom branding CSS retirement](https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/microsoft-entra-blog/microsoft-entra-id-enhances-security-of-branded-sign-ins/ba-p/4537471):** Direct IT to audit any custom CSS used on your Entra sign-in pages and complete necessary redesign before Microsoft retires CSS positioning properties, avoiding visible disruption to employee and partner sign-in experiences.

- **By September 2026 - [SharePoint auto-labeling preview evaluation](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=559105):** Engage your compliance team to prepare sensitivity label policies and test the auto-labeling preview so you can move to general availability in October with confidence that existing SharePoint data will be labeled consistently.

- **By August 2026 - [Teams app and agent management unification](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=567883):** Confirm your IT governance process is updated to reflect that app installation policies set in either the Microsoft 365 Admin Center or Teams Admin Center will now apply across both surfaces, preventing unintended app exposure.

*Sources: [Exchange Team Blog - July 2026 Security Updates](https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/exchange-team-blog/released-july-2026-exchange-server-security-updates/ba-p/4534146) · [Entra Blog - Enhanced Branded Sign-Ins](https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/microsoft-entra-blog/microsoft-entra-id-enhances-security-of-branded-sign-ins/ba-p/4537471) · [M365 Roadmap - SharePoint Auto-Labeling](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=559105)*

