## If You Take No Action

**Unpatched Exchange servers will remain exposed to known, documented vulnerabilities.** Microsoft published these security updates specifically because vulnerabilities were reported by external security partners, meaning the exploit details are effectively public. Every day an on-premises Exchange server runs without the July 2026 update is a day attackers with that knowledge can act. This is a direct HIPAA, SOC 2, and cyber insurance exposure.

**Employees in Teams are now being actively targeted and most are not aware of it.** Your workforce has been trained to recognize suspicious email. Phishing that arrives as a Teams chat from an external account looks entirely different and triggers none of those learned instincts. Without an update to your awareness program and external access policy review, attackers are operating in a channel where your defenses have not yet caught up.

**Unrestricted AI agent deployment without governance creates data exposure you cannot audit.** Agents that access enterprise content, call external tools, and take actions on behalf of users without runtime security controls create accountability gaps that are difficult to detect and harder to remediate after the fact. SOC 2 auditors and cyber insurers are beginning to ask specifically about AI agent governance; absence of a policy is increasingly a compliance finding, not just a risk.

